From 5dd54bbd286de2f501930689676896d427397d71 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Diego Pivoto <>
Date: Fri, 6 Nov 2026 10:12:17 -0300
Subject: [PATCH 5/6] fix(e2-kpm): report DRB measurements of the subscribed
 slice, per (UE, DRB)

The UE-level DRB measurements (DRB.UEThpDl/Ul, DRB.RlcSduDelayDl,
DRB.PdcpSduVolumeDL/UL) always read DRB 1, and the previous-report counters
were indexed by the subscription's UE index. With one S-NSSAI subscription
per slice and a phone holding a default PDU session plus a service session,
the service subscription read the idle DRB of the other session and the
subscriptions consumed each other's deltas (throughput and RLC delay 0).

The S-NSSAI matcher now keeps every DRB of the UE in the subscribed slice;
throughput and volume add their deltas, RLC delay takes the worst DRB, and
the counters (and the PRB-usage baselines) are kept per (UE, DRB). A DRB
without RLC/PDCP entity is skipped instead of asserting.
